# Agents

Operational rules for coding agents working in this repository.
Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` and `CONVENTIONS.md` first — they are the contract.

## Before you change anything

1. Locate the module or layer that owns the behaviour.
2. Read the existing code in that module; follow its patterns.
3. Check whether a shared utility already solves the problem.

## Hard rules

- Do not change the architecture. Extend the existing structure.
- Do not create abstractions with a single implementation.
- Do not add a dependency without stating why an existing one is insufficient.
- Do not bypass the dependency rules in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Do not modify infrastructure files (Dockerfile, compose, CI) unless the task
  is explicitly about infrastructure.
- Do not commit secrets. Configuration belongs in environment variables.
- Do not disable, skip or delete a test to make a build pass.
<% if (it.hasRepository) { -%>
- Do not import <%= it.config.orm %> outside the infrastructure layer.
<% } -%>

## When adding a feature

<% it.facts.addFeatureSteps.forEach(function (step, index) { -%>
<%= index + 1 %>. <%= step %>
<% }) -%>

## Commands

<% it.facts.commands.forEach(function (command) { -%>
- <%= command.label %>: `<%= command.command %>`
<% }) -%>

## Definition of done

A change is complete when it is implemented, tested, documented where behaviour
changed, and the full verification command passes.
<% if (it.facts.agentRules.length > 0) { -%>

## Project-specific rules

<% it.facts.agentRules.forEach(function (rule) { -%>
- <%= rule %>
<% }) -%>
<% } -%>
